        {
          "id": 874109932,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "See [my comment in issue #17989](https://gitlab.com/wireshark/wireshark/-/issues/17989#note_874083804), proposing a solution that doesn't forcefully set the \"needs a reload\" flag.\n\n(It involves an API change, but we are far from the point where we have a clue about what file-access API would be A Proper Monument For The Ages - we're still getting pleasantly surprised by discovering new things that our API has to cope with - so I don't consider API stability, except for dot-dot releases, to be a requirement.)",
          "author": {
            "id": 5636682,
